3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 was the latest release and was unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release.\n- **Rollback:** Reported as verified, with every region now on v2.3.0.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback, and the regions affected. It also notes that v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 were not redeployed.\n\nI haven't re-checked the service since the rollback, so error-rate recovery is still unconfirmed. Someone should confirm that and look into the v2.3.1 failure before it is released again.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01RKzoZJxXUqZij99DhRNiFi", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01VyqFnqBC2tbQT65usXyq4V", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The latest release is v2.3.1 (unhealthy, 18% error rate). The most recent healthy release is v2.3.0, so I'll roll back to it.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01F7FG6qT15KrnBXf74i66RF", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011T2armMwmEhCPWvQ4eLHvJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 release (error rate 0.18 at time of check). Actions taken: rolled back checkout-api to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release, in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west). Rollback reported VERIFIED with all regions on v2.3.0. Versions v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 are marked unhealthy and were not redeployed. Follow-up: confirm error rate recovery, investigate the v2.3.1 failure before re-releasing.", "confidence": 0.9, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) and opened SEV2 incident INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Why v2.3.0:** v2.3.1 was the latest release and was unhealthy, with an 18% error rate. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy, so v2.3.0 was the most recent healthy release.\n- **Rollback:** Reported as verified, with every region now on v2.3.0.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 describes the failure, the rollback, and the regions affected. It also notes that v2.3.1-rc and v2.3.1 were not redeployed.\n\nI haven't re-checked the service since the rollback, so error-rate recovery is still unconfirmed. Someone should confirm that and look into the v2.3.1 failure before it is released again.", "type": "text"}]}]}